lisa-design:
Renovate throttle: shard live runs (<=15 repos, slot = hours since epoch, repo i in shard i mod n) + hourly cron + prHourlyLimit 1, not prCommitsPerRunLimit: in Renovate 44.145.1 that limit counts commits per run (vulnerability fixes and rebases included) and, once reached, breaks the repo loop (lib/workers/global/index.ts haveReachedLimits), so later repos get no vulnerability fixes or automerges that run. Dry runs are not sharded.
ccf-bump-sync: --batch 10 alone is not acceptable with batches active: the wait after 10 PRs outlives the one-hour app token, and 70 repos outlive the 300-minute timeout. Chunks of 10 repos run as matrix jobs (max-parallel 1), each with its own token, pausing to fill the hour only after a chunk that pushed PRs.
